        ":question/id": "607151f7-a0f9-522f-b6fe-540456f7af54",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-50371",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $r(t)=\u27e8\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},\\,{t}^{5}\u27e9,$ ${r}^{\u2032}(t)=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}({e}^{t}+1)-{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={t}^{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}(t)=5{t}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8{x}^{\u2032}(t),\\,{y}^{\u2032}(t)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      }
    ]
  ],
